Python requirements originate from the OpenTelemetry Authors' Operator v0.160.0:
https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-operator/blob/v0.160.0/autoinstrumentation/python/requirements.txt

RIO modifies Python OTLP exporter 1.45.0 to preserve span/link W3C trace flags
alongside remote-parent flags. This backports the behavior proposed upstream:
https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-python/issues/4666
https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-python/pull/5667
The upstream Apache-2.0 source and package license remain in the payload.

The Ruby dependency graph was adapted from Grafana Beyla's Apache-2.0 image build,
with its OpenTelemetry Ruby source revision updated and locked:
https://github.com/grafana/beyla/tree/main/pkg/webhook/image/ruby

Bundled Injector and language agents are upstream OpenTelemetry distributions.
The Injector v0.11.0 Apache-2.0 license is preserved in
/licenses/upstream/injector/LICENSE (from its tagged upstream source).
Its Zig 0.15.2 standard-library MIT notice is preserved alongside it.
Supplemental native .NET dependency license texts are under
/licenses/upstream/dotnet; /licenses/upstream/manifest.json records immutable
sources and hashes. These materials do not complete the redistribution review.
Java's embedded META-INF/licenses material, .NET's LICENSE files, and the
Node.js, Python, and Ruby packages' license/notice files remain in /dist.
See THIRD_PARTY.md in the source distribution for the inventory, generated
notice snapshots, and outstanding review of embedded and base-image components.
